og/modal/popover elements and for text containing \\\"relationship\\\"/\\\"edge weight\\\" - none found. The only weight controls in the UI are per-node \\\"Weight\\\" sliders on each competency card, which are a separate value from the edge percentage labels (e.g. Programming Languages node Weight=90% while its outgoing edges show 80%/70%). There is no discoverable way to change a relationship/edge weight.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Enable/disable switch non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Clicking the \\\"Agile Methodology\\\" competency's enable/disable switch (both via Playwright's real click action and via direct JS .click() on the switch element) never changes its state: `aria-checked` remains \\\"true\\\" and `data-state` remains \\\"checked\\\" after every click attempt (tested 3 times in a row). The node card's visual styling also stays in the enabled state (green border-color, opacity:1) with no dimming/disabled indicator. Since the switch never toggles to the disabled state, the competency can never be excluded from Coverage/Critical Path/Risk Gap calculations via this control, so the exclusion behavior could not be verified either. (Note: a minor, likely unrelated metric drift from Coverage 68%->69% and Avg Level 3.3->3.4 was observed after the very first click, but it did not correspond to any visible disabled state and did not change further on subsequent clicks, so it cannot be attributed to a working disable action.)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library panel lists 5 templates (Software Engineer [Current], Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager), each showing role name, department/domain (Engineering, Product, Human Resources, Analytics, Sales), competency count (6 competencies each), relationship/connection count (5 connections each), and a set of descriptive keyword tags (e.g. programming/coding/software/development for Software Engineer; product/management/strategy/roadmap for Product Manager; hr/human resources/recruitment/talent for HR Manager; data/machine learning/analytics/statistics for Data Scientist; sales/revenue/business development/customer for Sales Manager). All fields needed for comparison are visible simultaneously without extra navigation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inconsistent state after template application - graph/nodes not updated\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Apply\\\" on the Product Manager template shows a \\\"Template Applied\\\" toast, updates the page title to \\\"Product Manager\\\", department to \\\"Product\\\", Coverage to 78%, Avg Level to 3.8, and Critical Path list to \\\"Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, +1\\\" (4 competencies), and the Scenario Simulation category-adjustment counts also update (technical 1 / behavioral 1 / leadership 1 / domain 3, summing to 6). However, the actual competency graph panel (node cards and edges) was NOT updated - it still displays the original Software Engineer competencies (Programming Languages, System Design, Code Review, Problem Solving, Collaboration, Agile Methodology) and the original 5 edges (prog-lang->code-review 80%, prog-lang->sys-design 70%, problem-solve->sys-design 90%, collab->code-review 60%, agile->collab 50%), none of which match the new Product Manager critical-path competency names (Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, etc). This is a direct inconsistency between the summary/metrics data and the rendered graph after applying a template.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Save-as-template missing name/description input and not retrievable afterward\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Save Current\\\" in the Template Library panel immediately shows a \\\"Template Saved\\\" toast (\\\"Current model configuration has been saved as a template.\\\") with no dialog/form prompting for a template name or description first - the action is a single click with no naming step at all. After the save, the Template Library list still shows only the original 5 templates (Software Engineer [Current], Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) - no new/duplicate template entry appears. A full-text search of the page also found no \\\"My Templates\\\" section anywhere. The saved template cannot be found or retrieved anywhere in the UI, so persistence/retrieval could not be verified and the naming/description requirement is not implemented.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each scenario tab shows a distinct title/description and distinct default Category Adjustment values: Recruitment = \\\"Recruitment Simulation / Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\" with all Level Change/Weight Change sliders at 0. Training = \\\"Training Simulation / Model the impact of training programs\\\" with technical Level Change +1, domain Level Change +1, others 0. Promotion = \\\"Promotion Simulation / Assess readiness for role advancement\\\" with technical Weight Change -5%, behavioral Weight Change +10%, others 0. Category competency counts (technical 3, behavioral 2, leadership 0, domain 1) remain consistent across tabs as expected since they reflect the same underlying model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Simulation produces NaN in Coverage metric\", \"actual\": \"Setting the \\\"technical\\\" category's Level Change slider to +2 (via keyboard ArrowRight while focused) caused the adjacent, untouched \\\"Weight Change\\\" slider for the same category to display \\\"NaN%\\\" instead of \\\"0%\\\" even before running the simulation. Clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" applied the adjustment: Avg Level correctly updated to 4.2/Advanced and Critical Path recalculated (same 3 competencies, reordered