        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 19, \"total_count\": 19, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Case-insensitive title match (software/DATA), description-fragment match (coordination -> Product Manager), department filter (Human Resources -> HR Manager only), and no-match query shows \\\"No jobs found\\\" empty state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Software Engineer\\\" card opened detail editor titled \\\"Software Engineer\\\" with Engineering/6 competencies, summary metrics (Coverage 68%, Avg Level 3.3, Critical Path 3, Risk Gaps 0), and a graph with 6 competency nodes and 5 edges matching the model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dragging the \\\"Programming Languages\\\" node to a new canvas position (~700,650) relocated the node (box moved from ~86,422 to ~582,585) while all 5 edges (prog-lang→code-review 80%, prog-lang→sys-design 70%, problem-solve→sys-design 90%, collab→code-review 60%, agile→collab 50%) remained present with unchanged endpoints and weights, confirming relationships stay correctly attached after rearrangement.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing functionality - no UI to edit edge/relationship weight\", \"actual\": \"Clicking an edge (e.g. \\\"Edge from prog-lang to code-review\\\", 80%) only toggles a CSS `selected` class on the SVG `<g>` element; no editable control, slider, input, panel, popover, or modal appears anywhere in the DOM. Double-click and right-click (contextmenu) produce no additional UI either. Inspected the edge's own outerHTML (1688 chars) - contains only SVG path/label elements, no interactive control. Searched full document for dialog/modal/popover elements and for text containing \\\"relationship\\\"/\\\"edge weight\\\" - none found. The only weight controls in the UI are per-node \\\"Weight\\\" sliders on each competency card, which are a separate value from the edge percentage labels (e.g. Programming Languages node Weight=90% while its outgoing edges show 80%/70%). There is no discoverable way to change a relationship/edge weight.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Enable/disable switch non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Clicking the \\\"Agile Methodology\\\" competency's enable/disable switch (both via Playwright's real click action and via direct JS .click() on the switch element) never changes its state: `aria-checked` remains \\\"true\\\" and `data-state` remains \\\"checked\\\" after every click attempt (tested 3 times in a row). The node card's visual styling also stays in the enabled state (green border-color, opacity:1) with no dimming/disabled indicator. Since the switch never toggles to the disabled state, the competency can never be excluded from Coverage/Critical Path/Risk Gap calculations via this control, so the exclusion behavior could not be verified either. (Note: a minor, likely unrelated metric drift from Coverage 68%->69% and Avg Level 3.3->3.4 was observed after the very first click, but it did not correspond to any visible disabled state and did not change further on subsequent clicks, so it cannot be attributed to a working disable action.)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library panel lists 5 templates (Software Engineer [Current], Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager), each showing role name, department/domain (Engineering, Product, Human Resources, Analytics, Sales), competency count (6 competencies each), relationship/connection count (5 connections each), and a set of descriptive keyword tags (e.g. programming/coding/software/development for Software Engineer; product/management/strategy/roadmap for Product Manager; hr/human resources/recruitment/talent for HR Manager; data/machine learning/analytics/statistics for Data Scientist; sales/revenue/business development/customer for Sales Manager). All fields needed for comparison are visible simultaneously without extra navigation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inconsistent state after template application - graph/nodes not updated\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Apply\\\" on the Product Manager template shows a \\\"Template Applied\\\" toast, updates the page title to \\\"Product Manager\\\", department to \\\"Product\\\", Coverage to 78%, Avg Level to 3.8, and Critical Path list to \\\"Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, +1\\\" (4 competencies), and the Scenario Simulation category-adjustment counts also update (technical 1 / behavioral 1 / leadership 1 / domain 3, summing to 6). However, the actual competency graph panel (node cards and edges) was NOT updated - it still displays the original Software Engineer competencies (Programming Languages, System Design, Code Review, Problem Solving, Collaboration, Agile Methodology) and the original 5 edges (prog-lang->code-review 80%, prog-lang->sys-design 70%, problem-solve->sys-design 90%, collab->code-review 60%, agile->collab 50%), none of which match the new Product Manager critical-path competency names (Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, etc). This is a direct inconsistency between the summary/metrics data and the rendered graph after applying a template.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Save-as-template missing name/description input and not retrievable afterward\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Save Current\\\" in the Template Library panel immediately shows a \\\"Template Saved\\\" toast (\\\"Current model configuration has been saved as a template.\\\") with no dialog/form prompting for a template name or description first - the action is a single click with no naming step at all. After the save, the Template Library list still shows only the original 5 templates (Software Engineer [Current], Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) - no new/duplicate template entry appears. A full-text search of the page also found no \\\"My Templates\\\" section anywhere. The saved template cannot be found or retrieved anywhere in the UI, so persistence/retrieval could not be verified and the naming/description requirement is not implemented.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each scenario tab shows a distinct title/description and distinct default Category Adjustment values: Recruitment = \\\"Recruitment Simulation / Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\" with all Level Change/Weight Change sliders at 0. Training = \\\"Training Simulation / Model the impact of training programs\\\" with technical Level Change +1, domain Level Change +1, others 0. Promotion = \\\"Promotion Simulation / Assess readiness for role advancement\\\" with technical Weight Change -5%, behavioral Weight Change +10%, others 0. Category competency counts (technical 3, behavioral 2, leadership 0, domain 1) remain consistent across tabs as expected since they reflect the same underlying model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Simulation produces NaN in Coverage metric\", \"actual\": \"Setting the \\\"technical\\\" category's Level Change slider to +2 (via keyboard ArrowRight while focused) caused the adjacent, untouched \\\"Weight Change\\\" slider for the same category to display \\\"NaN%\\\" instead of \\\"0%\\\" even before running the simulation. Clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" applied the adjustment: Avg Level correctly updated to 4.2/Advanced and Critical Path recalculated (same 3 competencies, reordered), but the Coverage metric became \\\"NaN%\\\" (a broken/invalid numeric display) instead of a valid percentage - this NaN clearly propagated from the corrupted Weight Change value into the coverage calculation. Clicking \\\"Reset\\\" did correctly restore Coverage to 68% and Avg Level to 3.3%, so Reset itself works, but the core \\\"adjust and run simulation\\\" flow produces an invalid/broken Coverage output, which is a functional defect.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Save does not persist model edits\", \"actual\": \"After dragging the \\\\\\\"Programming Languages\\\\\\\" node (~10-20px shift via arrow-key movement, node box previously at [86,422]) and clicking the top \\\\\\\"Save\\\\\\\" button - which showed a \\\\\\\"Model Saved - Your changes have been saved successfully\\\\\\\" toast - navigating away to the Models list and reopening \\\\\\\"Software Engineer\\\\\\\" shows the Programming Languages node back at its original box position [86,422,248,141], i.e. the edit was NOT persisted despite the success toast. All other metrics (Coverage 68%, Avg Level 3.3, Critical Path 3, Risk Gaps 0) also match the pristine original state, confirming the save action does not actually write changes to persisted storage - it only shows a false-positive success confirmation.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Level and Weight edit controls are non-functional, so bounds enforcement cannot be exercised/verified\", \"actual\": \"The per-competency Weight slider declares aria-valuemin=10 / aria-valuemax=100 (matching the expected 10%-100% spec) and the Level control is a 5-segment button bar (matching the expected 1-5/5 levels spec), but neither control actually responds to any interaction: (1) Playwright real click on the Level segment buttons toggles an [active] state marker but the underlying fill bar classes (bg-level-advanced/bg-muted) never change; (2) keyboard Arrow keys while the Weight slider has DOM focus are intercepted by React Flow's node keyboard-movement handler (moves the whole node instead, confirmed via ARIA live region \\\\\\\"Moved selected node left...\\\\\\\") because no nodrag/nopan isolation class exists on the slider or its ancestors; (3) a real Playwright mouse drag starting on the slider thumb resolves to a whole-node drag target (getByTestId('rf__node-prog-lang').dragTo(...)) rather than the slider, and produces no node movement or value change; (4) synthetic PointerEvent pointerdown/move/up dispatched directly at the track's rightmost edge (to seek toward max) also produces no aria-valuenow change (remained \\\\\\\"90\\\\\\\"). Since no interaction method can move the value at all, it is impossible to test whether attempting to exceed 100%/5 or go below 10%/1 is actually clamped/rejected by the app - the constraint cannot be verified due to this blocking control defect (consistent with the non-functional controls already identified in FT-11).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Coverage indicator updates in real time but to an invalid NaN value\", \"actual\": \"Adjusting only the technical category's Weight Change slider (via keyboard, 30->40 i.e. +10%) and clicking \\\\\\\"Run Simulation\\\\\\\" updates the Coverage/Avg Level summary immediately with no page reload (confirming the live-update mechanism itself fires), but the displayed values are corrupted: Coverage shows \\\\\\\"NaN%\\\\\\\" (progressbar aria-valuenow becomes null/removed) and Avg Level shows \\\\\\\"NaN\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"N/A\\\\\\\" instead of valid numbers. Root cause: merely focusing/adjusting the Weight Change slider corrupts the paired, untouched Level Change slider's value to \\\\\\\"NaN\\\\\\\" in the DOM even before running the simulation (same defect pattern as FT-10, here triggered in the reverse direction), and this NaN propagates into the real-time Coverage/Avg Level calculation once Run Simulation executes. So while updates happen immediately as required, the real-time coverage indicator does not correctly reflect the change - it displays a broken/invalid value.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On a freshly loaded model, the \\\"Recruitment\\\" scenario tab is selected by default with no prior tab interaction. Its panel is fully initialized: title \\\"Recruitment Simulation\\\", description \\\"Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\", and Category Adjustments section showing all 4 categories (technical 3, behavioral 2, leadership 0, domain 1 competencies) each with Level Change=0 and Weight Change=0% sliders, plus enabled \\\"Run Simulation\\\" and \\\"Reset\\\" buttons. Clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" immediately (without switching tabs first) succeeded, showing a \\\"Simulation Applied\\\" toast (\\\"Competency levels and weights have been adjusted based on the scenario.\\\") with no errors.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Using node position (the only functional graph edit control, since Level/Weight/enable controls are non-functional per FT-11/CS-12) as the test control: dragging \\\\\\\"Programming Languages\\\\\\\" from origin to translate(602px,727px), then dragging again to translate(969px,644px), showed the second drag's resulting position was a fresh offset from the first dragged position (not reset back to the original 0,0), confirming subsequent edits build on the current state rather than the stale/original one. Separately, the graph's per-node \\\\\\\"Critical\\\\\\\" badges (shown on Programming Languages, System Design, Problem Solving) exactly match the summary panel's Critical Path list (\\\\\\\"Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design\\\\\\\", count 3), and Risk Gaps shows \\\\\\\"0 identified\\\\\\\" with no risk indicators present on any node - confirming graph-level state and summary-level indicators agree with each 